hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27862","Sa'd ibn Ibrahim and Ya'qub narrated to us, they said: My father narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar ibn Abdillah ibn Hanzalah narrated to me, from Yusuf ibn Abdillah ibn Salam, from Khawlah bint Tha'labah, she said: By Allah, concerning me and Aws ibn Samit Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed the beginning of Surat al-Mujadalah. She said: I was with him, and he was an old man whose character had worsened and who had become fretful. She said: He came to me one day and I argued with him about something, so he became angry and said: You are to me as the back of my mother. She said: Then he went out and sat in his people's gathering for a while, then he came to me and desired me for himself. She said: So I said: No, by the One in whose Hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you shall not reach me after you said what you said until Allah and His Messenger judge concerning us with His judgment. She said: So he lunged at me and I resisted him, and I overcame him as a woman overcomes a weak old man, and I threw him off me. She said: Then I went out to one of my neighbors and borrowed clothes from her, then I went out until I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I sat before him and told him what I suffered from him, and I complained to him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of his bad character. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept saying: O Khuwaylah, your cousin is an old man, so fear Allah concerning him. She said: By Allah, I had not left before the Qur'an was revealed concerning me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was covered with what used to cover him, then it was lifted from him. So he said to me: O Khuwaylah, Allah has revealed concerning you and your companion. Then he recited to me: Allah has heard the statement of she who disputes with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah, and Allah hears your dialogue. Indeed Allah is Hearing, Seeing, up to His saying, and for the disbelievers is a painful punishment. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Command him to free a slave. She said: So I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he has nothing with which to free. He said: Then let him fast two consecutive months. She said: So I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man with no fasting in him. He said: Then let him feed sixty poor persons a wasq of dates. She said: I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he does not have that. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then we shall help him with a basket of dates. She said: So I said: And I, O Messenger of Allah, shall help him with another basket. He said: You have done right and well. Go and give charity on his behalf, then treat your cousin kindly. She said: So I did. Sa'd said: An araq is a basket."
